  },
  "description": "LTX-2.5 is an open-weights world model for video generation that generates multi-shot scenes in one pass, edits real footage, and exports cinema-grade EXR. Open weights you can fine-tune and run on your hardware.",
  "featureList": [
    "Cleaner motion with fewer artifacts",
    "Native multi-shot scene generation with character and environment continuity",
    "Better prompt adherence from shorter, simpler prompts",
    "Automatic duration adjustment",
    "Native 4K HDR generation",
    "Native RAW workflow support",
    "Fine-tunable pretrained foundation model",
    "Runs on consumer hardware including Mac",
    "Open weights available for download",
    "Free for commercial use under $10M ARR",
    "Generative editing of existing footage",
    "Multishot continuity across cuts",
    "Fast and light enough for real-time generation"
  ],
  "inLanguage": "en",
  "mainEntity": {
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "LTX-2.5 is the newest version of LTX, an open-weights world model for video generation. It's built as a stronger foundation, not just a new tool, that teams can build on, fine-tune, and deploy themselves."
        },
        "name": "What is LTX-2.5?"
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "It adds a better video decoder for cleaner motion, native multi-shot scenes that stay consistent across cuts, stronger prompt understanding, automatic clip duration, beta precise video editing, native 4K HDR and RAW support, and a faster, higher-quality distilled model."
        },
        "name": "What's new in LTX-2.5?"
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Yes. LTX-2.5 includes a pretrained base checkpoint built specifically for fine-tuning, so you can adapt it to your own domain and deploy it on your own infrastructure."
        },
        "name": "Can I fine-tune LTX-2.5 on my own data?"
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Self-hosted on 2× GB200 GPUs at 720p, LTX-2.5 generates a 10-second video clip in 6.8 seconds, which is faster than real time."
        },
        "name": "How fast is LTX-2.5?"
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "API pricing is billed per second of generated video. ltx-2-5-fast: $0.09/sec at 720p, $0.13/sec at 1080p, $0.19/sec at 1440p, and $0.30/sec at 4K. ltx-2-5-pro: $0.12/sec at 720p, $0.17/sec at 1080p, $0.25/sec at 1440p, and $0.39/sec at 4K. Full rates are on the API pricing page."
        },
        "name": "What does the LTX-2.5 API cost?"
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "LTX-2.5 uses open weights with a permissive license, no mandatory branding, and free use under $10M ARR."
        },
        "name": "What are the licensing terms for LTX-2.5?"
      }
    ]
  },
